  <!-- CONDITIONS -->
  <section id="conditions" class="reveal">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2>Active Conditions</h2><span class="count">10 tracked</span></div>

    <div class="card">
      <button class="acc-btn" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="num">1</span>
        <span class="ttl">BPPV — Left Posterior Canal<br><span class="badge b-good" style="margin-top:6px;">Resolved · monitor for recurrence</span></span>
        <span class="chev"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
      </button>
      <div class="acc-body"><div><div class="acc-inner">
        <p>Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo of the left posterior semicircular canal. Presented with spinning on turning over / rising from bed.</p>
        <p><strong>Diagnosed & treated</strong> by Dr. Abhinav Rai (ENT, Buxar) on 5 Jun 2026. Dix-Hallpike, Supine Roll and Deep Head Hanging tests confirmed left-sided BPPV (upbeating crescendo-decrescendo nystagmus, ~1 s latency, ~9 s duration).</p>
        <p><strong>Treatment:</strong> Epley maneuver in-clinic — immediate relief. Symptoms resolved.</p>
        <p><strong>Monitoring:</strong> Resolved but kept on watch — BPPV recurs in ~15–30% over 1–5 years. Watch for any return of positional spinning.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>This was the true cause of the episodes that triggered the May 2026 workup.</li>
          <li>If it recurs: return to Dr. Rai for repeat Epley (first line — not medication).</li>
          <li>Maintaining Vitamin D may lower recurrence risk.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <button class="acc-btn" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="num">2</span>
        <span class="ttl">Subclinical Hypothyroidism<br><span class="badge b-good" style="margin-top:6px;">Resolved · lifestyle</span></span>
        <span class="chev"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
      </button>
      <div class="acc-body"><div><div class="acc-inner">
        <p>TSH 4.81 (Sep 2025) → <strong>2.61 (May 2026)</strong> — normalized through exercise and diet. No medication.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Monitor with annual TSH.</li>
          <li>Anti-TPO not yet tested — consider if TSH rises again.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <button class="acc-btn" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="num">3</span>
        <span class="ttl">Vitamin B12 Deficiency<br><span class="badge b-treat" style="margin-top:6px;">Under treatment</span></span>
        <span class="chev"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
      </button>
      <div class="acc-body"><div><div class="acc-inner">
        <p>208.5 (Sep 2025) → <strong>194.5 pg/mL (May 2026)</strong>; ref 211–946. Worsening, now treated.</p>
